From smyth at wehi.edu.au  Sat Jul 30 15:55:18 2005
From: smyth at wehi.edu.au (Gordon Smyth)
Date: Sat, 30 Jul 2005 23:55:18 +1000
Subject: [BioC]  normalizing incomplete arrays [was: limma error message]
In-Reply-To: <mailman.1.1122717600.15548.bioconductor@stat.math.ethz.ch>
References: <mailman.1.1122717600.15548.bioconductor@stat.math.ethz.ch>
Message-ID: <6.2.1.2.1.20050730234659.0213cd28@imaphost.wehi.edu.au>

As you've deduced, the problem is that your arrays do not a constant block 
size. limma assumes a constant block size for normalizeWithinArrays() and 
imageplot().

Here is a work-around for GenePix data:

for (b in 1:48) {
         i <- RG$genes$Block==b
         MA2 <- normalizeWithinArrays(RG[i,],method="loess")
         if(b==1)
                 MA <- MA2
         else
                 MA <- rbind(MA,MA2)
}

This will perform print-tip-loess normalization even though there are 
irregular numbers of spots in the print-tip groups.

Gordon

